// Sources are split by the environment they run in. Each directory under src/
// has its own tsconfig.json extending this one, so no program sees another
// environment's globals, and an editor checks a file under the config nearest
// to it:
//
//   src/worker/  WebWorker globals. The Worker host runs in browser Workers and
//                in Node's worker_threads, so it uses nothing Node-specific.
//   src/page/    DOM globals.
//   src/node/    Node globals: harnesses.
//   src/shared/  no environment's globals, only the language. The other three
//                configs include it too, so their imports of it resolve.
//
// An environment statically imports only its own directory and src/shared/.
// Another environment's code is reached at run time by URL (a Worker script, a
// dynamic import()), because a static import would type-check it under the
// importer's globals. rootDir and outDir resolve against this file, so every
// config emits to dist/ with the layout of src/.
{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/tsconfig",
  "extends": "../../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist"
  }
}
